target/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
.tmp/
*.log

# Working notes for a session: screenshots, `uiautomator dump` output, one-off probes.
# Kept on disk because they answer "what did the screen actually look like", which is
# the one question a log cannot. Never worth a commit.
.workbuddy/

# The engineering log: 250 KB of protocol notes, measurements, dead ends and
# half-decided plans, written alongside the code and only useful next to it. A
# changelog records what shipped; this records what was being thought about.
# Kept on disk, kept out of the tree.
Task.md

# Release signing. The key already lives outside the tree; this keeps its password
# and any stray keystore that gets dropped in here from reaching the archive, where
# the only fix is rotating the key for every clone.
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Packet captures: 126 MB across seven files, and every question they can answer has
# already been turned into a number in the notes. The scripts that read them are worth
# a commit (they are the argument); the bytes underneath are not — GitHub refuses a
# single file over 100 MB anyway, and `t1-air.pcap` alone is 48.8 MB. Kept on disk,
# readable by the committed scripts, never in the tree.
*.pcap

# Python leaves these behind the first time anyone runs a probe.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
